        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: western Tasmania, South Africa\n- Products: Microcachrys, Protea\n- Concepts: endemic species, botanical names, common names\n\nFacts:\n- Microcachrys is endemic to western Tasmania.\n- Microcachrys is a low shrub that grows to 1 meter tall at high altitudes in western Tasmania.\n- Protea is a genus of South African flowering plants.\n- Protea is both the botanical name and the English common name for this genus.\n- Protea plants are sometimes also called sugarbushes, and in Afrikaans they are called suikerbos.",
